z(9,'prompt','An x86-64 denylist permits unmatched calls, blocks syscall 59, ignores arch, and runs on a kernel with i386 compatibility enabled. With valid i386 arguments, how could execve evade that one rule?','Compatibility/addressconditionsandallowdefault.',[sc])
z(9,'workedExample','The i386 execve number is 11 rather than native x86-64 number 59, so a denylist ignoring ABI can miss it. Validate supported ABIs and use correct per-ABI rules. Also handle x32 number encoding: x32 shares AUDIT_ARCH_X86_64 and sets __X32_SYSCALL_BIT, so checking arch alone is not enough. Existing threads also require correct filter synchronisation.','Criticalx32samearchnotfixedonlyarch.',[sc])
